    {
      "title": "ConfigMaps and Secrets: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ConfigMaps and Secrets: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What They Are",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ConfigMap",
                "Secret"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Holds",
                  "plain config",
                  "sensitive data"
                ],
                [
                  "Shape",
                  "key/value, strings or files",
                  "same"
                ],
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "namespaced",
                  "namespaced"
                ],
                [
                  "Extra",
                  "none",
                  "tmpfs on node, redacted in describe"
                ],
                [
                  "Stored",
                  "etcd",
                  "etcd"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Encoded, Not Encrypted",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==base64== is reversible encoding, no key",
                "Anyone who can **read** the Secret can decode it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "echo -n 'pw' | base64",
                "echo cHc= | base64 -d"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "cHc=",
                "pw"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Write and Protect",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`data:` = base64 values",
                "`stringData:` = plain text, converted on write, ==never returned==",
                "Pods consume both without an image rebuild",
                "At rest: `EncryptionConfiguration` on the API server (etcd)",
                "RBAC: restrict `get/list` on secrets",
                "Size limit ==1 MiB== per object"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Encrypted?** No, only base64-encoded.",
                "**Why not security?** Reversible, no key.",
                "**data vs stringData?** base64 vs plain, write-only.",
                "**1 MiB limit?** Keeps etcd and API server healthy."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Env Vars vs Mounted Files",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Env Vars vs Mounted Files",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Ways In",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One key: `env.valueFrom.configMapKeyRef` or `secretKeyRef`",
                "All keys: `envFrom`; value is ==fixed at container start==",
                "Volume: each key becomes a ==file== under `mountPath`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "envFrom:",
                "- configMapRef: {name: app}",
                "volumeMounts:",
                "- {name: sec, mountPath: /etc/db}",
                "volumes:",
                "- name: sec",
                "  secret: {secretName: db, defaultMode: 0400}"
              ],
              "note": "mount secrets as files, mode 0400"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Updates and Trade-offs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Env var",
                "Mounted file"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Live update",
                  "{red:never}, restart pod",
                  "{green:yes}, kubelet, up to ~1 min"
                ],
                [
                  "Exceptions",
                  "none",
                  "`subPath`, `immutable: true`"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "simple, 12-factor",
                  "secrets, big or multi-line, reload"
                ],
                [
                  "Leaks via",
                  "`kubectl exec env`, crash dumps",
                  "file mode"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Config changed?",
              "text": "Env needs `kubectl rollout restart deploy/app`; files refresh alone."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Env or volume for a DB password?** Volume: out of env dumps, `0400`",
                "**Running pod sees a ConfigMap change?** Files yes, env no",
                "**What does subPath break?** Automatic file refresh",
                "**Roll pods after a change?** `kubectl rollout restart deploy/app`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Namespaces: Scoping and Isolation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Namespaces: Scoping and Isolation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Namespace Basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Namespace== = virtual cluster partition; scopes **names**",
                "Defaults: `default`, `kube-system`, `kube-public`, `kube-node-lease`",
                "List cluster-scoped kinds: `kubectl api-resources --namespaced=false`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Namespaced",
                "Cluster-scoped"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "ConfigMap, Secret",
                  "Node"
                ],
                [
                  "Pod, Service, Role",
                  "PersistentVolume"
                ],
                [
                  "ServiceAccount",
                  "Namespace, ClusterRole, StorageClass"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Crossing Namespaces",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pod reads ConfigMap/Secret only from ==its own namespace==",
                "Needed elsewhere: **copy or recreate** the object per namespace",
                "Cross-namespace DNS: `svc.namespace.svc.cluster.local`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Not a Boundary",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Add"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Block traffic",
                  "`NetworkPolicy`"
                ],
                [
                  "Cap team usage",
                  "`ResourceQuota`, `LimitRange`"
                ],
                [
                  "Limit access",
                  "`RBAC`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set default: `kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=dev`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Cluster-scoped?** Node, PV, Namespace, ClusterRole, StorageClass",
                "**Pod in ns A mounts Secret from ns B?** No; copy it into A",
                "**Namespace isolates traffic?** No; add NetworkPolicy",
                "**Limit a team's resources?** ResourceQuota plus LimitRange"
              ],
              "style": "star",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "RBAC and Service Accounts Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "RBAC and Service Accounts Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Roles and Bindings",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Additive allow-only==: no deny rules",
                "Rule = `apiGroups`, `resources`, `verbs`",
                "Verbs: `get` `list` `watch` `create` `update` `patch` `delete`",
                "A binding grants a Role or ClusterRole to a User, Group or ServiceAccount"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Object",
                "Scope"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Role",
                  "one namespace"
                ],
                [
                  "ClusterRole",
                  "cluster-wide"
                ],
                [
                  "RoleBinding",
                  "==ONE namespace=="
                ],
                [
                  "ClusterRoleBinding",
                  "==cluster-wide=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Service Accounts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ServiceAccount== = pod identity; one `default` per namespace",
                "Set `spec.serviceAccountName`",
                "Short-lived projected token at `/var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount`",
                "No API calls: `automountServiceAccountToken: false`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Read ConfigMaps in dev",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl create role cm-reader --verb=get,list --resource=configmaps -n dev",
                "kubectl create rolebinding rb --role=cm-reader --serviceaccount=dev:app-sa -n dev",
                "kubectl auth can-i get secrets --as=system:serviceaccount:dev:app-sa -n dev"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "role.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/cm-reader created",
                "rolebinding.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/rb created",
                "no"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Least privilege",
              "text": "Avoid the `default` SA and `cluster-admin`. `list` on secrets returns **every value**, so grant it rarely."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Everyday Commands and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Everyday Commands and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Create and Inspect",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`--from-literal` sets one key; `--from-file` loads a file as a key",
                "`.data` holds ==base64==, so decode it with `base64 -d`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl create configmap app --from-literal=K=V --from-file=app.properties",
                "kubectl create secret generic db --from-literal=pw=s3cret",
                "kubectl get secret db -o jsonpath='{.data.pw}' | base64 -d"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Silent Failures",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`echo 'pw' | base64` adds a ==trailing newline==: password never matches",
                "Use `echo -n`, or `stringData`",
                "Env vars ==never update== in a running pod",
                "Missing key or object gives ==CreateContainerConfigError==; `optional: true` tolerates it"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Symptom",
                "Check",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CreateContainerConfigError",
                  "`kubectl describe pod` events",
                  "Create key/object, or `optional: true`"
                ],
                [
                  "Old config in pod",
                  "Pod started before change",
                  "`kubectl rollout restart deploy/app`"
                ],
                [
                  "403 Forbidden",
                  "`kubectl auth can-i`",
                  "Add a narrow Role + RoleBinding"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Security Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Secret YAML committed to ==Git==: base64 hides nothing",
                "==Default SA== left over-privileged",
                "`cluster-admin` or `*` verbs to silence Forbidden"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Fix Forbidden with the ==narrowest Role==. Create Secrets in the cluster, never from YAML in Git."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Config, Secrets, Namespaces, RBAC",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Config, Secrets, Namespaces, RBAC",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Config and Consume",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ConfigMap = ==plain== config; Secret = **base64**, not encrypted",
                "Add ==etcd encryption== + RBAC on secrets",
                "`data` base64, `stringData` plain",
                "Size limit ==1 MiB=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Env var",
                "Volume"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Syntax",
                  "`valueFrom`, `envFrom`",
                  "files in mountPath"
                ],
                [
                  "Updates",
                  "{red:static} until restart",
                  "{green:auto}, not subPath or immutable"
                ],
                [
                  "Secrets",
                  "visible in env",
                  "`defaultMode: 0400`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Scope and RBAC",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Kind",
                "Objects"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Namespaced",
                  "ConfigMap, Secret, Role, RoleBinding, ServiceAccount"
                ],
                [
                  "Cluster-scoped",
                  "ClusterRole, Node, PV"
                ],
                [
                  "One namespace",
                  "Role + RoleBinding"
                ],
                [
                  "All namespaces",
                  "ClusterRole + ClusterRoleBinding"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Least privilege==; **no deny rules**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl get cm -n dev",
                "kubectl get cm -A",
                "kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=dev",
                "kubectl auth can-i get secrets --as=system:serviceaccount:dev:app-sa -n dev"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**30 seconds:** Secret mounted as 0400 file, ServiceAccount with a Role for that secret only, etcd encrypted",
                "**Config unreadable?** 1) same namespace, key exists 2) pod events: CreateContainerConfigError 3) `can-i` as the SA"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A Secret was made from `echo 'pw' | base64`, and the app rejects the password. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`echo` adds a trailing newline, so the stored value decodes to `pw` plus a newline.",
                "Use `echo -n`, or write plain text under `stringData`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You edit a ConfigMap that feeds a pod through `envFrom`. Does the running pod see it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. Env vars are fixed at container start.",
                "Run `kubectl rollout restart deploy/app`. A mounted file would refresh, unless it uses `subPath`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`app-sa` has a RoleBinding to Role `cm-reader` (get, list configmaps) in `dev`. What does `can-i get configmaps -n prod` print?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`no`. A RoleBinding grants access in one namespace only.",
                "Nothing grants it in `prod`, and RBAC has no deny rules."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
